<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian '95 crude imports from Libya up 49.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Tunisian '95 crude imports from Libya up 49.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisin imports of Libyan crude oil amounted to 779,060 tonnes in 1995, up 49.5 percent from 521,050 a year earlier, official statistics showed.</p>
<p>Value of these imports from the neighbouring North African country amounted to $102 million, up 56.2 percent compared to $65 million.</p>
<p>The statistics were released by state-run oil company ETAP at the opening session of a four-day conference on oil exploration.</p>
<p>Imports of Syrian crude dropped to 40,620 tonnes from 104,400 tonnes.</p>
<p>Total crude oil imports in 1995 amounted to 854,560 tonnes, up 30.3 percent from 656.040 in 1994.</p>
<p>Total crude exports were 2.179 million tonnes in 1995, up 3.3 percent compared to 2.109 million tonnes in 1994.</p>
<p>-- Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
